Package: host-guardian
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/developerinlondon/host-guardian
Depends: @SHLIBS@systemd (>= 249)
Recommends: systemd-oomd, prometheus-node-exporter
Description: Host health guardian for mount identity and memory shedding
 host-guardian verifies that each declared mountpoint is still backed by the
 filesystem it is supposed to be, and stops operator-nominated units when the
 host is genuinely out of memory.
 .
 It is deliberately small. Memory, CPU, IO, load and filesystem metrics come
 from prometheus-node-exporter; restarting a failed unit is systemd's own
 Restart= directive; killing by cgroup pressure is systemd-oomd. host-guardian
 implements only what none of those cover: verifying that a mount is still the
 filesystem you declared, and shedding a *named* unit rather than whichever
 cgroup happens to be under the most pressure.
 .
 Results are published as a Prometheus textfile for node-exporter to collect,
 so host-guardian listens on no socket.
